L["Falconhurst was overrun — a hag had enslaved the village, and wicker monsters patrolled the streets. Inquisitor Cleardawn led the charge: you broke the hag's spell, freed the villagers, and held the barricade against waves of cursed attackers. Warren Ashton, the village blacksmith, remembered the old ways — weapons of silver and iron, blessed in ember. You forged an arsenal from his teachings and learned the most important lesson of all: the Drust feared fire. With blessed blades and burning brands, you were ready for the Crimsonwood."] = "Falconhurst was overrun — a hag had enslaved the village, and wicker monsters patrolled the streets. Inquisitor Cleardawn led the charge: you broke the hag's spell, freed the villagers, and held the barricade against waves of cursed attackers. Warren Ashton, the village blacksmith, remembered the old ways — weapons of silver and iron, blessed in ember. You forged an arsenal from his teachings and learned the most important lesson of all: the Drust feared fire. With blessed blades and burning brands, you were ready for the Crimsonwood."
