L["Lord Waycrest has vanished and a curse grips the village of Fallhaven. Lucille Waycrest enlists your help to hunt the witches responsible."] = "Lord Waycrest has vanished and a curse grips the village of Fallhaven. Lucille Waycrest enlists your help to hunt the witches responsible."
L["Lordaeron"] = "Lordaeron"
L["Lordaeron has been reclaimed, the penance accepted. But for those who once swore loyalty to the Banshee Queen, a message finds its way back through the dark — one last task, carried by a familiar messenger."] = "Lordaeron has been reclaimed, the penance accepted. But for those who once swore loyalty to the Banshee Queen, a message finds its way back through the dark — one last task, carried by a familiar messenger."
L["Lordaeron is in Forsaken hands again, but old enemies still haunt the forests beyond its walls. The Scarlet Crusade clings to its strongholds, Gilneas has not forgotten, and a former queen's absence leaves difficult questions behind.\n\nLilian Voss has a mission in Silverpine, and she needs someone who knows what it means to be Forsaken: to stand at a graveside, remember, and choose again what the second life is for."] = "Lordaeron is in Forsaken hands again, but old enemies still haunt the forests beyond its walls. The Scarlet Crusade clings to its strongholds, Gilneas has not forgotten, and a former queen's absence leaves difficult questions behind.\n\nLilian Voss has a mission in Silverpine, and she needs someone who knows what it means to be Forsaken: to stand at a graveside, remember, and choose again what the second life is for."
L["Lorewalker Cho"] = "Lorewalker Cho"
L["Lorewalker Cho did not answer Nazgrim's campaign with orders. He answered with tea, old stones, and the patient insistence that Pandaria had a story before the Horde arrived. You walked a mile in another person's shoes, listened to the forest's dead, peered into the past, and traced the branches of Cho's own family. The lesson was not gentle, but it was necessary: this land remembers what people bring into it. Then the river swallowed you, the hozen found you, and Chief Kah Kah's orders dragged the lesson back into the campaign. You left Cho with more questions than victories, which was probably the point."] = "Lorewalker Cho did not answer Nazgrim's campaign with orders. He answered with tea, old stones, and the patient insistence that Pandaria had a story before the Horde arrived. You walked a mile in another person's shoes, listened to the forest's dead, peered into the past, and traced the branches of Cho's own family. The lesson was not gentle, but it was necessary: this land remembers what people bring into it. Then the river swallowed you, the hozen found you, and Chief Kah Kah's orders dragged the lesson back into the campaign. You left Cho with more questions than victories, which was probably the point."
