L["Sire Denathrius pointed you at the Accuser, one of the Harvesters standing against him. Lord Chamberlain's hunt was brutal and theatrical: tear through her followers, read the sinstones of her inquisitors, and use those names to drag the guilty into judgment. But the deeper you went, the less clean the story became. The Accuser had punished pride for ages, and she understood what Denathrius's court had become. When her own secret was revealed, it was not simple innocence that saved her — it was the terrible truth that Revendreth's ruler had turned repentance into control."] = "Sire Denathrius pointed you at the Accuser, one of the Harvesters standing against him. Lord Chamberlain's hunt was brutal and theatrical: tear through her followers, read the sinstones of her inquisitors, and use those names to drag the guilty into judgment. But the deeper you went, the less clean the story became. The Accuser had punished pride for ages, and she understood what Denathrius's court had become. When her own secret was revealed, it was not simple innocence that saved her — it was the terrible truth that Revendreth's ruler had turned repentance into control."
