L["The second Horseman would be Thoras Trollbane, the warrior-king of Stromgarde who had been murdered by his own son. You traveled to the ruined kingdom where Trollbane's restless spirit lingered, betrayed even in death. Prince Galen, the traitor-son, stood in your way — but regicide was a small price for the Ebon Blade. You cut Galen down and raised his father, and Thoras Trollbane rode once more, his fury undimmed by centuries in the grave."] = "The second Horseman would be Thoras Trollbane, the warrior-king of Stromgarde who had been murdered by his own son. You traveled to the ruined kingdom where Trollbane's restless spirit lingered, betrayed even in death. Prince Galen, the traitor-son, stood in your way — but regicide was a small price for the Ebon Blade. You cut Galen down and raised his father, and Thoras Trollbane rode once more, his fury undimmed by centuries in the grave."
