L["Search the wrecked raft in Un'Goro and bring the small pack to Linken at Marshal's Refuge."] = "Search the wrecked raft in Un'Goro and bring the small pack to Linken at Marshal's Refuge."
L["Follow the next names in Linken's tale and prepare the totem he will need."] = "Follow the next names in Linken's tale and prepare the totem he will need."
L["Seek Haleh in Winterspring and bring her General Drakkisath's blood to make the Drakefire Amulet."] = "Seek Haleh in Winterspring and bring her General Drakkisath's blood to make the Drakefire Amulet."
L["Seek Loramus Thalipedes in Azshara. The demon hunter knows how Razelikh is warded, but he needs a name torn from the deep."] = "Seek Loramus Thalipedes in Azshara. The demon hunter knows how Razelikh is warded, but he needs a name torn from the deep."
L["Seek Strahad Farsan, assemble the Tome of the Cabal, and prepare the felhunter binding."] = "Seek Strahad Farsan, assemble the Tome of the Cabal, and prepare the felhunter binding."
L["Seek the earth's sapta, speak with its manifestation, and return with your first totem."] = "Seek the earth's sapta, speak with its manifestation, and return with your first totem."
L["Seek the halves of the pendant across lake and sea so the form of the sea lion may be taught."] = "Seek the halves of the pendant across lake and sea so the form of the sea lion may be taught."
L["Seek the Islander, gather the charms, and answer Bath'rah's summons for the whirlwind weapon."] = "Seek the Islander, gather the charms, and answer Bath'rah's summons for the whirlwind weapon."
L["Sentinel Elissa's missing scout was alive, but Balthule's report was grave. Warlocks held the tower, their parchments spoke of the Dark Strand, and the warning had to reach Ashenvale."] = "Sentinel Elissa's missing scout was alive, but Balthule's report was grave. Warlocks held the tower, their parchments spoke of the Dark Strand, and the warning had to reach Ashenvale."
L["Shaw's report gave Gryan a name, but the messenger gave him movement. The Defias Traitor then led you through Moonbrook to the hidden entrance beneath the ruined town."] = "Shaw's report gave Gryan a name, but the messenger gave him movement. The Defias Traitor then led you through Moonbrook to the hidden entrance beneath the ruined town."
L["Speak with the proper trainer and bind the felsteed that will carry you on darker roads."] = "Speak with the proper trainer and bind the felsteed that will carry you on darker roads."
L["Sven's murdered family and Jitters' fear showed that Raven Hill was being worked by a darker hand. With Morbent's Bane prepared, you ended the necromancer beyond the graves."] = "Sven's murdered family and Jitters' fear showed that Raven Hill was being worked by a darker hand. With Morbent's Bane prepared, you ended the necromancer beyond the graves."
L["Tabetha's work asked for texts, materials, and a measure of field sense. When the ritual was complete, your studies had a proper focus in hand."] = "Tabetha's work asked for texts, materials, and a measure of field sense. When the ritual was complete, your studies had a proper focus in hand."
L["Take Coleman's concern to Magistrate Sevren and descend into the crypt beneath the mills."] = "Take Coleman's concern to Magistrate Sevren and descend into the crypt beneath the mills."
L["Take Johaan's work to Silverpine, recover Berard's research, and bring Faranell the samples he requires."] = "Take Johaan's work to Silverpine, recover Berard's research, and bring Faranell the samples he requires."
L["Take the soggy clue at its word and look for the next scrap where the riddle says it waits."] = "Take the soggy clue at its word and look for the next scrap where the riddle says it waits."
L["The Agamand Mills still bore the family name, though the family itself had joined Tirisfal's dead. You brought Coleman Farthing the remains he asked for and helped clear the grounds for Brill."] = "The Agamand Mills still bore the family name, though the family itself had joined Tirisfal's dead. You brought Coleman Farthing the remains he asked for and helped clear the grounds for Brill."
L["The amulet hunt sent you after pieces, components, and summoned echoes in dangerous places. Each recovery brought Lord Valthalak's broken pride closer to being called forth."] = "The amulet hunt sent you after pieces, components, and summoned echoes in dangerous places. Each recovery brought Lord Valthalak's broken pride closer to being called forth."
L["The Ancient Petrified Leaf proved to be a summons. The ancients named the demons, and by hunting them alone you earned the right to carry Rhok'delar."] = "The Ancient Petrified Leaf proved to be a summons. The ancients named the demons, and by hunting them alone you earned the right to carry Rhok'delar."
L["The Armory and Cathedral were the Crusade's creed made flesh. Houndmaster Loksey guarded the Library with trained violence. Herod turned recruits into zealots through spectacle and blood. In the Cathedral, Scarlet Commander Mograine and High Inquisitor Whitemane embodied the order's shining lie: holy words wrapped around endless war. Whether sent by Varimathras or Raleigh, you cut through the Monastery's saints and executioners alike."] = "The Armory and Cathedral were the Crusade's creed made flesh. Houndmaster Loksey guarded the Library with trained violence. Herod turned recruits into zealots through spectacle and blood. In the Cathedral, Scarlet Commander Mograine and High Inquisitor Whitemane embodied the order's shining lie: holy words wrapped around endless war. Whether sent by Varimathras or Raleigh, you cut through the Monastery's saints and executioners alike."
L["The Azsharite was raw possibility: crystal from a dangerous coast, named by a demon hunter, and meant for a foe normal steel could not touch. Galvan the Ancient gave that possibility form. Felbane was not an heirloom or a trophy. It was a blade for one brutal task: wound Razelikh's protected servants, gather the shattered amulet, and open the way to the demon himself."] = "The Azsharite was raw possibility: crystal from a dangerous coast, named by a demon hunter, and meant for a foe normal steel could not touch. Galvan the Ancient gave that possibility form. Felbane was not an heirloom or a trophy. It was a blade for one brutal task: wound Razelikh's protected servants, gather the shattered amulet, and open the way to the demon himself."
L["The blue shard hid grave purpose beneath impossible errands. Azuregos sent you to Narain, and Narain's ledger demanded Molten Core goggles, a great chimaerok meal, a stolen book, a ransom drop, pages from dragons, the fires of Onyxia and Ragnaros, and Neptulon's wrath off Azshara's coast. Strange as it was, each step pulled the shard closer to the scepter."] = "The blue shard hid grave purpose beneath impossible errands. Azuregos sent you to Narain, and Narain's ledger demanded Molten Core goggles, a great chimaerok meal, a stolen book, a ransom drop, pages from dragons, the fires of Onyxia and Ragnaros, and Neptulon's wrath off Azshara's coast. Strange as it was, each step pulled the shard closer to the scepter."
L["The call of air was brief, but it completed what the earlier trials began. Earth, fire, water, and air now stood with you."] = "The call of air was brief, but it completed what the earlier trials began. Earth, fire, water, and air now stood with you."
L["The call of water sent you farther than the earlier trials. Through Barrens dust and distant roads, you learned the patience the element required."] = "The call of water sent you farther than the earlier trials. Through Barrens dust and distant roads, you learned the patience the element required."
L["The charger's trial demanded sacrifice, craft, and courage in haunted places. At the end, the spirit answered the Light and came to your side."] = "The charger's trial demanded sacrifice, craft, and courage in haunted places. At the end, the spirit answered the Light and came to your side."
L["The Circle sent you from lesson to remedy. You found the source of the sickness, gathered the cure, and restored creatures that had been left to suffer."] = "The Circle sent you from lesson to remedy. You found the source of the sickness, gathered the cure, and restored creatures that had been left to suffer."
L["The Dalaran wizards at Ambermill were moving supplies and waking old ley-work beneath Silverpine. Shadow Priest Allister and Dalar Dawnweaver followed the evidence until Archmage Ataeric stood exposed."] = "The Dalaran wizards at Ambermill were moving supplies and waking old ley-work beneath Silverpine. Shadow Priest Allister and Dalar Dawnweaver followed the evidence until Archmage Ataeric stood exposed."
L["The dead of Darrowshire rose to fight again. You held the line, faced the corrupted Joseph Redpath, and gave Pamela the peace of knowing her father had come home."] = "The dead of Darrowshire rose to fight again. You held the line, faced the corrupted Joseph Redpath, and gave Pamela the peace of knowing her father had come home."
L["The Deadmines were mine, factory, shipyard, and fortress. At the heart of it all stood Edwin VanCleef, whose death ended Westfall's immediate crisis and left one final letter behind."] = "The Deadmines were mine, factory, shipyard, and fortress. At the heart of it all stood Edwin VanCleef, whose death ended Westfall's immediate crisis and left one final letter behind."
L["The device revealed Anthion Harmon, a ghost bound by his sister's danger. You entered Stratholme, reached Ysida in time, and returned to the brother who had waited outside its gates."] = "The device revealed Anthion Harmon, a ghost bound by his sister's danger. You entered Stratholme, reached Ysida in time, and returned to the brother who had waited outside its gates."
L["The Elixir of Agony passed from blossom to composite, from Faranell's decay to Lydon's final activation. With Dun Garok stout as the vessel, the inn itself became the last test."] = "The Elixir of Agony passed from blossom to composite, from Faranell's decay to Lydon's final activation. With Dun Garok stout as the vessel, the inn itself became the last test."
L["The Fallen Hero speaks of a regiment lost waiting for orders. Begin in Stonard and search the southern swamps for the command that never reached him."] = "The Fallen Hero speaks of a regiment lost waiting for orders. Begin in Stonard and search the southern swamps for the command that never reached him."
L["The Fallen Hero's grief began with obedience. He led his soldiers toward the Blasted Lands and waited for orders that never came. Dispatch Commander Ruag remembered the lost message, Bengor remembered the ambush, and the Swamp Talker still held the Warchief's command. The truth was bitter: the regiment had been told to withdraw. The order never reached them."] = "The Fallen Hero's grief began with obedience. He led his soldiers toward the Blasted Lands and waited for orders that never came. Dispatch Commander Ruag remembered the lost message, Bengor remembered the ambush, and the Swamp Talker still held the Warchief's command. The truth was bitter: the regiment had been told to withdraw. The order never reached them."
L["The felsteed was not purchased like an ordinary mount. It was called, bound, and made to bear the one who mastered the ritual."] = "The felsteed was not purchased like an ordinary mount. It was called, bound, and made to bear the one who mastered the ritual."
L["The fight moved from ghostly remorse to demon-hunter craft. Loramus Thalipedes understood Razelikh's ward, but knowledge had to be earned. Lord Arkkoroc gave up the beast's name only after Hetaera's heads were brought from the Bay of Storms, and Loramus used the blood to name the enemy properly. The demon's protections were no longer a mystery. Felbane had to be made."] = "The fight moved from ghostly remorse to demon-hunter craft. Loramus Thalipedes understood Razelikh's ward, but knowledge had to be earned. Lord Arkkoroc gave up the beast's name only after Hetaera's heads were brought from the Bay of Storms, and Loramus used the blood to name the enemy properly. The demon's protections were no longer a mystery. Felbane had to be made."
L["The final clue led to the great falls on the Hinterlands coast. Under the water, after pirates, mud, and raptors, Cortello's chest waited with a reward fit for a traveler."] = "The final clue led to the great falls on the Hinterlands coast. Under the water, after pirates, mud, and raptors, Cortello's chest waited with a reward fit for a traveler."
L["The final proof came from General Drakkisath himself. His blood completed the amulet's power, and Rexxar turned the long road of commands, disguises, skulls, and trials into a single key. The Horde had its answer to Onyxia: strength tested across the world and deep inside Blackrock Spire."] = "The final proof came from General Drakkisath himself. His blood completed the amulet's power, and Rexxar turned the long road of commands, disguises, skulls, and trials into a single key. The Horde had its answer to Onyxia: strength tested across the world and deep inside Blackrock Spire."
L["The first binding taught the warlock's bargain clearly. A creature of the void answered, resisted, and was made to serve."] = "The first binding taught the warlock's bargain clearly. A creature of the void answered, resisted, and was made to serve."
L["The first Defias were thieves in the vineyards and bandits on the roads. By the time Morgan the Collector's ring reached Marshal Dughan, the red masks looked less like chance and more like organization."] = "The first Defias were thieves in the vineyards and bandits on the roads. By the time Morgan the Collector's ring reached Marshal Dughan, the red masks looked less like chance and more like organization."
L["The first exchange began with a worn class bracer and a simple test of readiness. Deliana or Mokvar made the first improvement and sent you onward to Gadgetzan."] = "The first exchange began with a worn class bracer and a simple test of readiness. Deliana or Mokvar made the first improvement and sent you onward to Gadgetzan."
L["The first scroll waited in the hold of a Bloodsail ship with no one to explain it. Its verse led you beneath a bridge in the Swamp of Sorrows, where the next clue lay in the mud."] = "The first scroll waited in the hold of a Bloodsail ship with no one to explain it. Its verse led you beneath a bridge in the Swamp of Sorrows, where the next clue lay in the mud."
L["The first signs of Onyxia's reach came from the Burning Steppes, where Helendis Riverhorn watched black dragonkin gathering strength. Magistrate Solomon treated the threat as a kingdom matter, Bolvar Fordragon weighed it from Stormwind Keep, and Marshal Maxwell became the Alliance's field anchor. The question was no longer whether dragons were moving. It was who in Stormwind had allowed the threat to spread."] = "The first signs of Onyxia's reach came from the Burning Steppes, where Helendis Riverhorn watched black dragonkin gathering strength. Magistrate Solomon treated the threat as a kingdom matter, Bolvar Fordragon weighed it from Stormwind Keep, and Marshal Maxwell became the Alliance's field anchor. The question was no longer whether dragons were moving. It was who in Stormwind had allowed the threat to spread."
L["The Graveyard and Library showed the Crusade's order from the inside. Vorrel Sengutz lay tortured by Interrogator Vishas. Scholars wanted books the Crusade had locked away. Horde agents wanted the Compendium of the Fallen, and Parqual Fintallas wanted the book the Crusade used to teach itself how to fight the dead. Alliance scholars wanted the Mythology of the Titans. Every shelf and cell told the same truth: the Scarlet Crusade did not only kill enemies. It controlled what its followers were allowed to know."] = "The Graveyard and Library showed the Crusade's order from the inside. Vorrel Sengutz lay tortured by Interrogator Vishas. Scholars wanted books the Crusade had locked away. Horde agents wanted the Compendium of the Fallen, and Parqual Fintallas wanted the book the Crusade used to teach itself how to fight the dead. Alliance scholars wanted the Mythology of the Titans. Every shelf and cell told the same truth: the Scarlet Crusade did not only kill enemies. It controlled what its followers were allowed to know."
L["The green shard was not won by simple killing. Eranikus had fallen into nightmare, and Remulos needed the corruption named before it could be answered. The defense of Moonglade became a rite before all who came to stand there: shades pouring from the Dream, Remulos holding the line, and Tyrande's grace turning a dragon's rage toward redemption."] = "The green shard was not won by simple killing. Eranikus had fallen into nightmare, and Remulos needed the corruption named before it could be answered. The defense of Moonglade became a rite before all who came to stand there: shades pouring from the Dream, Remulos holding the line, and Tyrande's grace turning a dragon's rage toward redemption."
L["The Horde's road to Onyxia began with Blackrock command papers and the old wound of the Blackhand name. Warlord Goretooth demanded proof from Lower Blackrock Spire, Eitrigg weighed the report in Orgrimmar, and Thrall sent you to kill Warchief Rend Blackhand. Rend's death was a declaration that the Horde would not bow to a false warchief propped up by dragons."] = "The Horde's road to Onyxia began with Blackrock command papers and the old wound of the Blackhand name. Warlord Goretooth demanded proof from Lower Blackrock Spire, Eitrigg weighed the report in Orgrimmar, and Thrall sent you to kill Warchief Rend Blackhand. Rend's death was a declaration that the Horde would not bow to a false warchief propped up by dragons."
L["The Islander tested your mettle, Bath'rah named the charms, and Cyclonian answered the call. When the storm was defeated, the weapon was yours."] = "The Islander tested your mettle, Bath'rah named the charms, and Cyclonian answered the call. When the storm was defeated, the weapon was yours."
L["The last climb belonged to the dead as much as the living. Grol the Destroyer, Archmage Allistarj, and Lady Sevine each held a piece of Razelikh's power, and Felbane made them mortal enough to fall. The united ward opened the Rise of the Defiler. There, above the ruined land that had swallowed a Horde regiment, Razelikh finally answered for the souls he chained. The Fallen Hero could not undo his failure, but he saw the demon broken and his soldiers released."] = "The last climb belonged to the dead as much as the living. Grol the Destroyer, Archmage Allistarj, and Lady Sevine each held a piece of Razelikh's power, and Felbane made them mortal enough to fall. The united ward opened the Rise of the Defiler. There, above the ruined land that had swallowed a Horde regiment, Razelikh finally answered for the souls he chained. The Fallen Hero could not undo his failure, but he saw the demon broken and his soldiers released."
L["The last preparations made the brazier ready. After ghosts, goblins, gladiators, and dungeon shades, the path narrowed to the chamber where Valthalak could answer."] = "The last preparations made the brazier ready. After ghosts, goblins, gladiators, and dungeon shades, the path narrowed to the chamber where Valthalak could answer."
L["The last step was not to kill Yenniku, but to reach him. At the Ruins of Aboraz, beside Zanzil's servants and the haunted Crystal Shore, the Soul Gem turned violence into rescue. Yenniku's soul was pulled free of Zanzil's control and carried back to Nimboya. The work that had begun with trophies and cauldron smoke ended as a Darkspear promise: the tribe would remember the one who brought the chief's son home."] = "The last step was not to kill Yenniku, but to reach him. At the Ruins of Aboraz, beside Zanzil's servants and the haunted Crystal Shore, the Soul Gem turned violence into rescue. Yenniku's soul was pulled free of Zanzil's control and carried back to Nimboya. The work that had begun with trophies and cauldron smoke ended as a Darkspear promise: the tribe would remember the one who brought the chief's son home."
L["The notice at Westbrook Garrison named a gnoll and a claw. Forest's Edge taught the rest. Hogger stood among the Riverpaw with enough strength to make a simple bounty feel like a hard lesson in the wilds beyond Elwynn's roads. When Marshal Dughan received the claw, the border toward Westfall felt less like open countryside and more like a warning."] = "The notice at Westbrook Garrison named a gnoll and a claw. Forest's Edge taught the rest. Hogger stood among the Riverpaw with enough strength to make a simple bounty feel like a hard lesson in the wilds beyond Elwynn's roads. When Marshal Dughan received the claw, the border toward Westfall felt less like open countryside and more like a warning."
L["The Plaguelands proved the Crusade had become more than a monastery. Scarlet banners flew over towers and towns, Stratholme's living quarter hid the Fordring family painting, and Hearthglen stood as a fortress of certainty. Tirion Fordring, exiled and alone, still believed his son could be saved from it. Forgotten memories, lost honor, and the painting became weapons against fanatic teaching. Disguised as Scarlet, you reached Taelan and watched him remember who he was before the Crusade taught him whom to hate."] = "The Plaguelands proved the Crusade had become more than a monastery. Scarlet banners flew over towers and towns, Stratholme's living quarter hid the Fordring family painting, and Hearthglen stood as a fortress of certainty. Tirion Fordring, exiled and alone, still believed his son could be saved from it. Forgotten memories, lost honor, and the painting became weapons against fanatic teaching. Disguised as Scarlet, you reached Taelan and watched him remember who he was before the Crusade taught him whom to hate."
L["The raft in Un'Goro held a compass, a curled map, a lion-headed key, and a photograph of a gnome in green. Linken knew the belongings, but memory would not come with them. The crater had left him with fragments of an errand, a blade without its tale, and the sense that someone had once entrusted him with more than he could remember."] = "The raft in Un'Goro held a compass, a curled map, a lion-headed key, and a photograph of a gnome in green. Linken knew the belongings, but memory would not come with them. The crater had left him with fragments of an errand, a blade without its tale, and the sense that someone had once entrusted him with more than he could remember."
L["The records, letters, and keepsakes led from Duskwood to Stormwind, Elwynn, Westfall, and back again. At Mistmantle Manor, Stalvan's legend ended with his ring in Madame Eva's hands."] = "The records, letters, and keepsakes led from Duskwood to Stormwind, Elwynn, Westfall, and back again. At Mistmantle Manor, Stalvan's legend ended with his ring in Madame Eva's hands."
L["The red shard was the bluntest path and perhaps the cruelest. Vaelastrasz, already broken by Nefarian, could only point toward the master of Blackwing Lair and set a clock running. The shard was taken from Nefarian under pressure, a raid victory folded into the long duty of the scepter."] = "The red shard was the bluntest path and perhaps the cruelest. Vaelastrasz, already broken by Nefarian, could only point toward the master of Blackwing Lair and set a clock running. The shard was taken from Nefarian under pressure, a raid victory folded into the long duty of the scepter."
L["The red tear outside Ahn'Qiraj was memory made visible. Anachronos let the past speak: the night elves, dragons, and qiraji locked in a war old enough to feel mythic. The scepter had broken across dragonflights and tragedies. To open the gates, the champion would have to follow those wounds into the Emerald Dream, Blackwing Lair, and Azshara's blue-dragon riddles."] = "The red tear outside Ahn'Qiraj was memory made visible. Anachronos let the past speak: the night elves, dragons, and qiraji locked in a war old enough to feel mythic. The scepter had broken across dragonflights and tragedies. To open the gates, the champion would have to follow those wounds into the Emerald Dream, Blackwing Lair, and Azshara's blue-dragon riddles."
L["The second clue turned the riddle into a journey across the sea. In Dustwallow, among Bloodfen raptors, another scrap waited for anyone stubborn enough to keep reading."] = "The second clue turned the riddle into a journey across the sea. In Dustwallow, among Bloodfen raptors, another scrap waited for anyone stubborn enough to keep reading."
L["The Stockade did not end the matter. Thelwater's visitor, Baros' warning, Shaw's caution, and Trias' quiet knowledge all pointed toward a dangerous friend of the Brotherhood inside Stormwind."] = "The Stockade did not end the matter. Thelwater's visitor, Baros' warning, Shaw's caution, and Trias' quiet knowledge all pointed toward a dangerous friend of the Brotherhood inside Stormwind."
L["The succubus trial warned that not every danger arrives with brute force. You gathered what was required and bound temptation to command."] = "The succubus trial warned that not every danger arrives with brute force. You gathered what was required and bound temptation to command."
L["The Sunken Temple trial asked you to carry the elements as one calling. When the proofs were gathered, your mastery had been tested in full."] = "The Sunken Temple trial asked you to carry the elements as one calling. When the proofs were gathered, your mastery had been tested in full."
L["The Tome of the Cabal led through old contacts and dangerous errands. When the binding was done, the felhunter's hunger became your weapon against magic."] = "The Tome of the Cabal led through old contacts and dangerous errands. When the binding was done, the felhunter's hunger became your weapon against magic."
L["The Tome of Valor led you to Daphne Stilwell and a hard lesson in service. Valor was not spoken over you; it was proven on a dangerous road."] = "The Tome of Valor led you to Daphne Stilwell and a hard lesson in service. Valor was not spoken over you; it was proven on a dangerous road."
L["The trail began beneath the broken Thandol Span, beside a dwarf pinned in the riverbed. Sully Balloo's letter was not a weapon, a map, or a royal order. It was a husband's goodbye, written before war turned private love into public loss. Sara Balloo received the letter in Ironforge and asked for only one thing more: that her king know what had been given in his name."] = "The trail began beneath the broken Thandol Span, beside a dwarf pinned in the riverbed. Sully Balloo's letter was not a weapon, a map, or a royal order. It was a husband's goodbye, written before war turned private love into public loss. Sara Balloo received the letter in Ironforge and asked for only one thing more: that her king know what had been given in his name."
L["The water trial carried you beyond the safety of your trainer. When the pendant was made whole, the sea lion form answered, and deeper waters opened to you."] = "The water trial carried you beyond the safety of your trainer. When the pendant was made whole, the sea lion form answered, and deeper waters opened to you."
L["The Woodpaw trail looked at first like scavenging. Then you found Raschal's backpacks pinned to a tree, still bearing Feathermoon insignia. One parcel could be delivered to Thalanaar, a small duty completed in the middle of the search. The other evidence mattered more: a note about strange insect creatures south of the gnoll camps. Raschal had not merely been attacked. He had chosen to investigate a threat under Feralas."] = "The Woodpaw trail looked at first like scavenging. Then you found Raschal's backpacks pinned to a tree, still bearing Feathermoon insignia. One parcel could be delivered to Thalanaar, a small duty completed in the middle of the search. The other evidence mattered more: a note about strange insect creatures south of the gnoll camps. Raschal had not merely been attacked. He had chosen to investigate a threat under Feralas."
L["The worgen were another fear in the dark, hunting through grove and orchard. Calor tested you against them until Master Carevin accepted that you could help keep their teeth from Darkshire."] = "The worgen were another fear in the dark, hunting through grove and orchard. Calor tested you against them until Master Carevin accepted that you could help keep their teeth from Darkshire."
L["The Writhing Deep made the whole case larger. Raschal was alive, sealed inside an alien pod by the Zukk'ash, and his report confirmed that Feralas was facing something more dangerous than a local hive. Shandris Feathermoon sent the warning to Darnassus, where Gracina Spiritmight named the threat: silithid. What began as a missing courier ended as an early warning about the insect menace waiting beneath Azeroth's southern deserts."] = "The Writhing Deep made the whole case larger. Raschal was alive, sealed inside an alien pod by the Zukk'ash, and his report confirmed that Feralas was facing something more dangerous than a local hive. Shandris Feathermoon sent the warning to Darnassus, where Gracina Spiritmight named the threat: silithid. What began as a missing courier ended as an early warning about the insect menace waiting beneath Azeroth's southern deserts."
L["Theldren's challengers waited in the Ring of Law, where words meant little. You survived the arena, and Anthion had what he needed for the next pieces."] = "Theldren's challengers waited in the Ring of Law, where words meant little. You survived the arena, and Anthion had what he needed for the next pieces."
L["Theramore brought the mystery into the open without solving it. Commander Samaul sent you to Sentry Point, Archmage Tervosh guided you to Private Hendel, and Hendel's guard post became the last fight of the trail. When Hendel yielded, Jaina Proudmoore appeared to take charge of the prisoner and thank you quietly for services that could not be publicly named. You had exposed the kidnapping of King Varian Wrynn, but the larger wound remained open: the king was still missing, and someone powerful enough to use the Defias had not yet shown their face."] = "Theramore brought the mystery into the open without solving it. Commander Samaul sent you to Sentry Point, Archmage Tervosh guided you to Private Hendel, and Hendel's guard post became the last fight of the trail. When Hendel yielded, Jaina Proudmoore appeared to take charge of the prisoner and thank you quietly for services that could not be publicly named. You had exposed the kidnapping of King Varian Wrynn, but the larger wound remained open: the king was still missing, and someone powerful enough to use the Defias had not yet shown their face."
L["Thomas sends you quietly to Bishop DeLavey in Stormwind Keep, where a missing envoy has become a private matter."] = "Thomas sends you quietly to Bishop DeLavey in Stormwind Keep, where a missing envoy has become a private matter."
L["Tirion Fordring asks for aid in a personal matter that leads through Stratholme and Scarlet-held country."] = "Tirion Fordring asks for aid in a personal matter that leads through Stratholme and Scarlet-held country."
L["Travel to Moonglade, hear the Great Bear Spirit, and return ready for the trial of body and heart."] = "Travel to Moonglade, hear the Great Bear Spirit, and return ready for the trial of body and heart."
L["Trias sends you into Old Town after Dashel Stonefist, whose answers pull the matter beyond Stormwind."] = "Trias sends you into Old Town after Dashel Stonefist, whose answers pull the matter beyond Stormwind."
L["Turn from worgen to Dalaran, gathering crates, pendants, and rune-work around Ambermill."] = "Turn from worgen to Dalaran, gathering crates, pendants, and rune-work around Ambermill."
L["Turn stolen Scarlet orders against Tyr's Hand and use Nathanos' disguise to walk inside their ranks."] = "Turn stolen Scarlet orders against Tyr's Hand and use Nathanos' disguise to walk inside their ranks."
L["Tyrion's disguise and spybot drew Lord Gregor Lescovar and Marzon the Silent Blade into the open. Their deaths carried the truth back through Trias, Baros, and the king's court."] = "Tyrion's disguise and spybot drew Lord Gregor Lescovar and Marzon the Silent Blade into the open. Their deaths carried the truth back through Trias, Baros, and the king's court."
L["Use Dartol's Rod to reach Krolg and turn against Ran Bloodtooth's corrupted furbolg."] = "Use Dartol's Rod to reach Krolg and turn against Ran Bloodtooth's corrupted furbolg."
L["Use Mux's device near Stratholme, then race the city to save Ysida Harmon from the baron."] = "Use Mux's device near Stratholme, then race the city to save Ysida Harmon from the baron."
L["Carry Kin'weelay's Soul Gem into the jungle and look for the moment to free Yenniku."] = "Carry Kin'weelay's Soul Gem into the jungle and look for the moment to free Yenniku."
L["Use the taming rod on the beasts your trainer names, then return to learn how to keep a companion."] = "Use the taming rod on the beasts your trainer names, then return to learn how to keep a companion."
L["Follow Linken's memory through strange visions and help his sword remember what he cannot."] = "Follow Linken's memory through strange visions and help his sword remember what he cannot."
L["Vaelastrasz gives little time for ceremony. The red shard must be claimed before the chance is lost."] = "Vaelastrasz gives little time for ceremony. The red shard must be claimed before the chance is lost."
L["VanCleef's letter reached Baros Alexston, who remembered the Stonemasons better than most. His concern led to Warden Thelwater, Bazil Thredd, and the riot within the Stockade."] = "VanCleef's letter reached Baros Alexston, who remembered the Stonemasons better than most. His concern led to Warden Thelwater, Bazil Thredd, and the riot within the Stockade."
L["When the shards were whole, the matter no longer belonged to one champion. The Might of Kalimdor waited on the war effort, the armies at the wall, and all who had prepared for the gates to open. The gong turned a repaired scepter into history: Ahn'Qiraj opened, and the war beyond the Scarab Wall began."] = "When the shards were whole, the matter no longer belonged to one champion. The Might of Kalimdor waited on the war effort, the armies at the wall, and all who had prepared for the gates to open. The gong turned a repaired scepter into history: Ahn'Qiraj opened, and the war beyond the Scarab Wall began."
L["When your hunter trainer turns from weapons to trust, learn how to tame and train a beast. Later, if an ancient leaf ever finds its way into your hands, answer the stranger calling from Felwood."] = "When your hunter trainer turns from weapons to trust, learn how to tame and train a beast. Later, if an ancient leaf ever finds its way into your hands, answer the stranger calling from Felwood."
L["When your old dungeon armor has seen enough battle, Deliana or Mokvar will offer work that sounds simple enough: bring the right pieces, prove you are ready, and keep following instructions.\n\nThe errands soon reach far beyond a single set of bracers. Expect old dungeons, stranger patrons, expensive favors, and a brazier whose purpose is not explained all at once."] = "When your old dungeon armor has seen enough battle, Deliana or Mokvar will offer work that sounds simple enough: bring the right pieces, prove you are ready, and keep following instructions.\n\nThe errands soon reach far beyond a single set of bracers. Expect old dungeons, stranger patrons, expensive favors, and a brazier whose purpose is not explained all at once."
L["Win Theldren's challenge in Blackrock Depths so Anthion can continue the armor work."] = "Win Theldren's challenge in Blackrock Depths so Anthion can continue the armor work."
L["With Athrikus Narassin weakened, Balthule sent you back into Althalaxx. You climbed past the warlocks of the Dark Strand and ended their master where he had gathered them."] = "With Athrikus Narassin weakened, Balthule sent you back into Althalaxx. You climbed past the warlocks of the Dark Strand and ended their master where he had gathered them."
L["With Felbane in hand, follow the last names the Fallen Hero gives you and prepare for the demon's reckoning."] = "With Felbane in hand, follow the last names the Fallen Hero gives you and prepare for the demon's reckoning."
L["With Onyxia exposed, the Alliance still needed a way into her lair. Bolvar sent you to Haleh, hidden in Winterspring, and Haleh named the final price: the blood of General Drakkisath from Upper Blackrock Spire. The black dragonflight's own champion became the material for the Drakefire Amulet. The court conspiracy was over. The assault on Onyxia could begin."] = "With Onyxia exposed, the Alliance still needed a way into her lair. Bolvar sent you to Haleh, hidden in Winterspring, and Haleh named the final price: the blood of General Drakkisath from Upper Blackrock Spire. The black dragonflight's own champion became the material for the Drakefire Amulet. The court conspiracy was over. The assault on Onyxia could begin."
L["With the Eye of Divinity in hand, seek Eris Havenfire and protect the spirits entrusted to you."] = "With the Eye of Divinity in hand, seek Eris Havenfire and protect the spirits entrusted to you."
L["With the three shards restored, take up the Scepter of the Shifting Sands and return to the Scarab Gong."] = "With the three shards restored, take up the Scepter of the Shifting Sands and return to the Scarab Gong."
L["You answered the call to Moonglade and learned from the Great Bear Spirit. When the final trial was done, the strength of the bear was yours to call upon in battle."] = "You answered the call to Moonglade and learned from the Great Bear Spirit. When the final trial was done, the strength of the bear was yours to call upon in battle."
L["You approached the wild as a hunter must: with patience, caution, and respect. When the final beast yielded, you were no longer meant to travel alone."] = "You approached the wild as a hunter must: with patience, caution, and respect. When the final beast yielded, you were no longer meant to travel alone."
L["You carried ore, gems, and other hard-won materials back to Jordan Stilwell. Verigan's Fist was not granted by ceremony alone; it was made through effort."] = "You carried ore, gems, and other hard-won materials back to Jordan Stilwell. Verigan's Fist was not granted by ceremony alone; it was made through effort."
L["You carried the sapta, listened to the earth, and proved steady enough to bear its totem. The first element had answered."] = "You carried the sapta, listened to the earth, and proved steady enough to bear its totem. The first element had answered."
L["You returned to the one who started the work with a full trail behind you: rescues, bargains, spirits, and old dungeons. The final pieces made the upgraded set a record of where you had been."] = "You returned to the one who started the work with a full trail behind you: rescues, bargains, spirits, and old dungeons. The final pieces made the upgraded set a record of where you had been."
L["Your first warrior lesson was not about striking harder. You learned to take the blow, hold your ground, and live long enough to answer."] = "Your first warrior lesson was not about striking harder. You learned to take the blow, hold your ground, and live long enough to answer."
L["Your mage trainer sends you to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh, where practical magic begins with travel, errands, and materials that will not gather themselves.\n\nFollow the lessons that turn study into tools: a wand, a strange polymorph, and food enough for hungry companions."] = "Your mage trainer sends you to Tabetha in Dustwallow Marsh, where practical magic begins with travel, errands, and materials that will not gather themselves.\n\nFollow the lessons that turn study into tools: a wand, a strange polymorph, and food enough for hungry companions."
L["Your poison training taught the trade plainly: enter unseen, open what is locked, and survive the danger you mean to wield."] = "Your poison training taught the trade plainly: enter unseen, open what is locked, and survive the danger you mean to wield."
