L["Korgran still called himself caretaker of Mourning Rise, even as Urtago quietly did more and more of the work. Together you cleared kobolds from the memorial, recovered what they had stolen, and saw how often Korgran lost the thread of the present. The duties that defined him were slipping away.\n\nWhen the time came, Korgran chose one more tradition. He forged a lantern, searched for a lost earthen, cleaned ashes from the memorial, and walked toward the coast with Urtago beside him. His farewell was not treated as defeat. It was a final act of care, made in the place he had guarded for so long."] = "Korgran still called himself caretaker of Mourning Rise, even as Urtago quietly did more and more of the work. Together you cleared kobolds from the memorial, recovered what they had stolen, and saw how often Korgran lost the thread of the present. The duties that defined him were slipping away.\n\nWhen the time came, Korgran chose one more tradition. He forged a lantern, searched for a lost earthen, cleaned ashes from the memorial, and walked toward the coast with Urtago beside him. His farewell was not treated as defeat. It was a final act of care, made in the place he had guarded for so long."
